 1239:    // An example of how to use these functions is:
 1240:    //   
 1241:    //    getNodalValues(L, &Node::compZCoord, zLAtNodes);
 1242:    // 
 1243:    // Where L is the level at which the field is to be interpolated. The field can be either
 1244:    // a double (depth), an array (u[nvrt]), or a function that depends on the level (Node::compZCoord(int k)). 
 1245:    // There are different versions of getNodalValues for each of these cases.
